  "title": "Szabo-2026-neurons-10.1038/s41467-026-71502-z",
  "description": "Intraoperative local field potential (LFP) recordings from the subthalamic nucleus of 13 patients with Parkinson's disease undergoing deep brain stimulation surgery. Recordings were made with microelectrodes during a stop-signal reaction time task, which probes action cancellation and response inhibition. This derivative release provides the authors' filtered 250 Hz continuous LFP, repackaged in BIDS with task events.",
  "methods_description": "Intraoperative microelectrode LFP was recorded from the STN while patients performed a stop-signal task. The authors' EEGLAB files at 250 Hz, high-pass filtered at 0.5 Hz, were converted to BrainVision float32 µV with unchanged values. Annotations were written to events.tsv.",
